#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:2
msgid "Reading and writing"
msgstr "Läsa och skriva"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:4
msgid ""
"Files live on disk; Python reaches them through :func:`open`, which returns "
"a *file object* whose methods read and write the underlying bytes."
msgstr ""
"Filer ligger på disk; Python når dem genom :func:`open`\\ , som returnerar "
"ett *filobjekt* vars metoder läser och skriver de underliggande bytena."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:9
msgid "open and modes"
msgstr "open och lägen"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:11
msgid ""
"The first argument is the path; the second is the *mode* -- a short string "
"telling Python how the file will be used:"
msgstr ""
"Det första argumentet är sökvägen; det andra är *läget* -- en kort sträng "
"som talar om för Python hur filen ska användas:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:14
msgid "``\"r\"`` -- read (default). Opens an existing file for reading."
msgstr "``\"r\"`` -- läsning (standard). Öppnar en befintlig fil för läsning."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:15
msgid ""
"``\"w\"`` -- write. Creates a new file or *truncates* an existing one to "
"empty."
msgstr ""
"``\"w\"`` -- skrivning. Skapar en ny fil eller *trunkerar* en befintlig till"
" tom."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:17
msgid ""
"``\"a\"`` -- append. Opens a file for writing at its end without truncating."
msgstr ""
"``\"a\"`` -- tillägg. Öppnar en fil för skrivning vid dess slut utan att "
"trunkera."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:19
msgid ""
"``\"b\"`` appended to any of the above (``\"rb\"``, ``\"wb\"``, ``\"ab\"``) "
"-- binary mode. The file's contents are :class:`bytes` rather than "
":class:`str`."
msgstr ""
"``\"b\"`` tillagt till något av ovanstående (\\ ``\"rb\"``\\ , ``\"wb\"``\\ "
", ``\"ab\"``\\ ) -- binärt läge. Filens innehåll är :class:`bytes` snarare "
"än :class:`str`\\ ."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:30
msgid "Use a context manager"
msgstr "Använd en kontexthanterare"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:32
msgid ""
"The pattern above leaks the file handle if anything between :func:`open` and"
" ``close`` raises. The fix is the ``with`` statement (see :doc:`context "
"managers <../classes/context-managers>`):"
msgstr ""
"Mönstret ovan läcker filhandtaget om något mellan :func:`open` och ``close``"
" kastar. Lösningen är ``with``\\ -satsen (se :doc:`kontexthanterare "
"<../classes/context-managers>`\\ ):"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:43
msgid "This is the standard form -- write it this way every time."
msgstr "Detta är standardformen -- skriv det så här varje gång."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:46
msgid "Reading"
msgstr "Läsning"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:48
msgid "File objects support several read styles:"
msgstr "Filobjekt stöder flera lässtilar:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:50
msgid ""
":meth:`io.IOBase.read` -- read the whole file (or N bytes) and return it as "
"a single string (or bytes object)."
msgstr ""
":meth:`io.IOBase.read` -- läs hela filen (eller N byte) och returnera den "
"som en enda sträng (eller bytes-objekt)."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:52
msgid ""
":meth:`io.IOBase.readline` -- read one line, including the trailing "
"``\"\\n\"``."
msgstr ""
":meth:`io.IOBase.readline` -- läs en rad, inklusive den avslutande "
"``\"\\n\"``\\ ."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:54
msgid ""
"Iterating the file directly yields lines one at a time, with much smaller "
"memory use than reading the whole file at once."
msgstr ""
"Att iterera filen direkt ger rader en i taget, med mycket mindre "
"minnesanvändning än att läsa hela filen på en gång."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:63
msgid ""
":meth:`str.rstrip` removes the trailing newline before printing so the "
"output is not double-spaced."
msgstr ""
":meth:`str.rstrip` tar bort den avslutande radbrytningen före utskrift så "
"att utdatan inte blir dubbelt radavstånd."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:67
msgid "Writing"
msgstr "Skrivning"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:69
msgid "Open the file in ``\"w\"`` mode and use :meth:`io.IOBase.write`:"
msgstr "Öppna filen i läget ``\"w\"`` och använd :meth:`io.IOBase.write`\\ :"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:77
msgid ""
":meth:`io.IOBase.write` does *not* add a newline -- it writes exactly the "
"bytes (or characters, in text mode) you give it."
msgstr ""
":meth:`io.IOBase.write` lägger *inte* till en radbrytning -- den skriver "
"exakt de byte (eller tecken, i textläge) du ger den."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:81
msgid "Text vs binary"
msgstr "Text kontra binärt"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:83
msgid ""
"Text mode (default, ``\"r\"`` / ``\"w\"`` without ``\"b\"``) decodes "
"incoming bytes into :class:`str` using a default encoding, and encodes "
"outgoing :class:`str` back to bytes. Use it for configuration, logs, JSON --"
" anything that *is* text."
msgstr ""
"Textläge (standard, ``\"r\"`` / ``\"w\"`` utan ``\"b\"``\\ ) avkodar "
"inkommande byte till :class:`str` med en standardkodning, och kodar utgående"
" :class:`str` tillbaka till byte. Använd det för konfiguration, loggar, JSON"
" -- allt som *är* text."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:88
msgid ""
"Binary mode (``\"rb\"`` / ``\"wb\"``) skips the decode step and returns "
":class:`bytes`. Use it for images, struct-packed records, network captures "
"-- anything where every byte matters and the file is not human-readable."
msgstr ""
"Binärt läge (\\ ``\"rb\"`` / ``\"wb\"``\\ ) hoppar över avkodningssteget och"
" returnerar :class:`bytes`\\ . Använd det för bilder, struct-packade poster,"
" nätverksinfångningar -- allt där varje byte spelar roll och filen inte är "
"läsbar för människor."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:94
msgid "Listing and removing files"
msgstr "Lista och ta bort filer"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:96
msgid ""
"The :mod:`os` module exposes the filesystem operations that are not on the "
"file object itself:"
msgstr ""
"Modulen :mod:`os` exponerar filsystemsoperationerna som inte finns på själva"
" filobjektet:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:99
msgid ":func:`os.listdir` -- returns a list of names in a directory."
msgstr ":func:`os.listdir` -- returnerar en lista med namn i en katalog."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:100
msgid ":func:`os.remove` -- delete a file."
msgstr ":func:`os.remove` -- ta bort en fil."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:101
msgid ":func:`os.rename` -- rename a file."
msgstr ":func:`os.rename` -- byt namn på en fil."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:102
msgid ":func:`os.stat` -- file metadata (size, modification time, ...)."
msgstr ":func:`os.stat` -- filmetadata (storlek, ändringstid, ...)."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:104
msgid ":func:`os.mkdir` -- create a new directory."
msgstr ":func:`os.mkdir` -- skapa en ny katalog."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/files-and-data/reading-and-writing.rst:113
msgid ""
"Catch :exc:`OSError` around these when the file or directory may not be "
"there -- the operation is one of the common places exceptions show up in "
"real scripts."
msgstr ""
"Fånga :exc:`OSError` runt dessa när filen eller katalogen kanske inte finns "
"-- operationen är ett av de vanliga ställena där undantag dyker upp i "
"verkliga skript."
